
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="zh-Hant-TW">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>相似詞解釋</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Sans+TC:wght@400;500;700&family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@600;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#EDF1EE; --paper:#FAFBF9; --ink:#1E2833; --muted:#5B6873; --rule:#C8D2CB;
  --a:#0E6A66; --a-soft:#D6EAE6; --b:#7A3B6C; --b-soft:#EEDDEA; --ok:#2F7A3A; --no:#A63A2B;
  --serif:"Noto Serif TC","Songti TC","PMingLiU",serif;
  --sans:"Noto Sans TC","PingFang TC","Microsoft JhengHei",system-ui,sans-serif;
  box-sizing:border-box;
  padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px); padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px);
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --bg:#141A1F; --paper:#1C242B; --ink:#E6ECEF; --muted:#9AA7B1; --rule:#33404A;
    --a:#6FC7BF; --a-soft:#1E3533; --b:#D59AC7; --b-soft:#3A2536; --ok:#7CCB86; --no:#EE8B7C;
  }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#141A1F; --paper:#1C242B; --ink:#E6ECEF; --muted:#9AA7B1; --rule:#33404A;
  --a:#6FC7BF; --a-soft:#1E3533; --b:#D59AC7; --b-soft:#3A2536; --ok:#7CCB86; --no:#EE8B7C;
}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:inherit}
html{scroll-padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px)}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--sans);line-height:1.65;font-size:16px}
.wrap{max-width:980px;margin:0 auto;padding:28px 20px 64px}
h1{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:900;font-size:clamp(28px,5vw,40px);margin:0 0 4px;letter-spacing:.04em}
.sub{color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 24px}

.ask{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto;gap:12px;align-items:center;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:14px}
.ask input{width:100%;font:600 24px var(--serif);padding:10px 14px;border-radius:10px;border:2px solid var(--rule);background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);text-align:center}
#wa{border-color:var(--a)} #wb{border-color:var(--b)}
.ask input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:2px}
.vs{font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--muted);font-size:20px}
button{font:inherit;cursor:pointer}
.go{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 22px;font-weight:700;font-size:17px}
.go:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:wait}
button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--a);outline-offset:2px}
@media (max-width:640px){.ask{grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr}.go{grid-column:1/-1}}

.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:14px 0 0}
.chip{background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--ink);border-radius:999px;padding:5px 14px;font-size:15px}
.chip[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border-color:var(--ink)}
.chip.custom{border-style:dashed}

.status{margin:18px 0 0;color:var(--muted);min-height:1.5em}
.status.err{color:var(--no)}

/* result */
.face{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin-top:28px;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden}
.side{padding:22px 24px}
.side.a{background:var(--a-soft)} .side.b{background:var(--b-soft)}
.word{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:900;font-size:clamp(44px,9vw,76px);line-height:1.1;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.a .word{color:var(--a)} .b .word{color:var(--b)}
.py{font:500 17px var(--sans);color:var(--muted)}
.gloss{font-weight:700;margin:6px 0 0}
.shared{grid-column:1/-1;background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:14px 24px}
.shared b{font-family:var(--serif)}
.en{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px;display:block}
.pyl{display:block;font-size:14.5px;color:var(--ink);opacity:.7;letter-spacing:.01em}
body.nopy .pyl{display:none}
.contrast .pyl{color:inherit}
.tools{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;margin-top:10px}
.pytog{background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--ink);border-radius:8px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:14px}
.pytog[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border-color:var(--ink)}

h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:22px;margin:36px 0 12px}
.cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}
@media (max-width:640px){.face,.cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.col{background:var(--paper);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 18px;border-left:5px solid var(--a)}
.col.b{border-left-color:var(--b)}
.col h3{margin:0 0 8px;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:20px}
.col.a h3{color:var(--a)} .col.b h3{color:var(--b)}
.col ul{margin:0;padding-left:1.1em}
.col li{margin:0 0 10px}

.ex{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0}
.ex li{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--rule)}
.ex li:last-child{border-bottom:0}
.ex .zh{font-size:18px}
mark{background:none;font-weight:700;padding:0 1px}
mark.ma{color:var(--a);box-shadow:inset 0 -.35em var(--a-soft)}
mark.mb{color:var(--b);box-shadow:inset 0 -.35em var(--b-soft)}
.say{flex:none;border:1px solid var(--rule);background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);border-radius:50%;width:34px;height:34px;display:grid;place-items:center;margin-top:2px}
.say svg{width:16px;height:16px}

.contrast{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 24px;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--serif);display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start}
.contrast .en{color:inherit;opacity:.75;font-family:var(--sans)}
.contrast .say{background:transparent;color:var(--paper);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.35)}
.contrast mark.ma,.contrast mark.mb{color:inherit;box-shadow:inset 0 -.12em currentColor}

.swap{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:grid;gap:10px}
.swap li{background:var(--paper);border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:28px 1fr;gap:10px}
.swap .zh{display:block}
.mk{font-weight:700;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}
.mk.ok{color:var(--ok)} .mk.no{color:var(--no)}
.swap .zh{font-size:17px}
.swap .zh.no{text-decoration:line-through;text-decoration-color:var(--no)}

.quiz{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:grid;gap:14px;counter-reset:q}
.quiz>li{background:var(--paper);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 18px;counter-increment:q}
.quiz .qs{font-size:19px;display:flex;gap:10px}
.quiz .qs::before{content:counter(q) ".";color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;padding-top:3px}
.blank{display:inline-block;min-width:3.2em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--muted);text-align:center;margin:0 3px;font-weight:700}
.blank.done{border-bottom-color:transparent}
.quiz .pyl{margin-left:1.6em}
.opts{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:12px 0 0 1.6em}
.opt{border:2px solid var(--rule);background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);border-radius:10px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px}
.opt.oa{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:700;color:var(--a);border-color:var(--a)}
.opt.ob{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:700;color:var(--b);border-color:var(--b)}
.opt:disabled{cursor:default;opacity:.45}
.opt.right{opacity:1;background:var(--ok);border-color:var(--ok);color:#fff}
.opt.wrong{opacity:1;background:var(--no);border-color:var(--no);color:#fff}
.fb{margin:10px 0 0 1.6em;font-size:15px}
.fb b.ok{color:var(--ok)} .fb b.no{color:var(--no)}
.score{margin-top:16px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:18px}
.again{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:0;border-radius:8px;padding:8px 16px;font-weight:700}
.ai-note{margin-top:28px;font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:12px}
.empty{margin-top:40px;color:var(--muted);text-align:center}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.face{animation:in .35s ease-out}@keyframes in{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(6px)}}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>相似詞解釋</h1>
  <p class="sub">輸入兩個詞，看看差別在哪裡。<span class="en">Type two similar words to see how they differ, with example sentences.</span></p>

  <div class="ask" role="search">
    <input id="wa" aria-label="第一個詞 first word" placeholder="清楚" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off">
    <span class="vs" aria-hidden="true">／</span>
    <input id="wb" aria-label="第二個詞 second word" placeholder="明確" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off">
    <button class="go" id="go">比較</button>
  </div>
  <div class="chips" id="chips" aria-label="常見詞組 saved pairs"></div>
  <div class="tools"><button class="pytog" id="pytog" aria-pressed="true">拼音 Pinyin</button></div>
  <p class="status" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

  <div id="out"><p class="empty">點上面的詞組，或輸入你自己的兩個詞。<span class="en">Tap a pair above, or type your own.</span></p></div>
</div>

<script>
const P = [
{a:"看書",b:"唸書",pa:"kàn shū",pb:"niàn shū",ga:"to read (a book)",gb:"to study; to be in school",
 shared:{zh:"都跟「書」和學習有關。",en:"Both involve books, but only 唸書 means studying as a task or being enrolled in school."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"單純「讀」的動作，休閒、工作都可以。",en:"The plain act of reading, for fun or for work."},{zh:"讀的是什麼都可以：小說、雜誌、報告。",en:"Any reading material: novels, magazines, reports."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"為了考試、課業而「讀」，有任務感。",en:"Studying for a test or class, with a goal attached."},{zh:"也可以指「上學、在某地求學」（台灣常用）。",en:"Also means attending school somewhere (common in Taiwan)."}],
 exA:[{zh:"我週末喜歡在咖啡廳看書，放鬆一下。",en:"On weekends I like to read at a café and unwind."},{zh:"她每個月至少看兩本跟領導力有關的書。",en:"She reads at least two leadership books a month."}],
 exB:[{zh:"她以前在西雅圖唸書，畢業後進了科技公司。",en:"She studied in Seattle, then joined a tech company after graduating."},{zh:"下週要考證照，這幾天我都在家唸書。",en:"My certification exam is next week, so I've been studying at home."}],
 contrast:{zh:"我不是在唸書，只是在看小說而已。",en:"I'm not studying, I'm just reading a novel."},
 swap:[{zh:"他在台大看書。",ok:false,en:"Wrong if you mean \"he's a student at NTU.\" Use 唸書."},{zh:"我在房間看書／唸書。",ok:true,en:"Both work. 唸書 suggests schoolwork; 看書 is any reading."}]},

{a:"資訊",b:"消息",pa:"zīxùn",pb:"xiāoxi",ga:"information, data",gb:"news, word (about something happening)",
 shared:{zh:"都是「得到的訊息」。",en:"Both refer to something you learn, but 資訊 is facts/data and 消息 is news about an event or person."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"客觀的資料、知識，偏正式、書面。",en:"Objective facts or data; more formal."},{zh:"常搭配：蒐集、提供、查詢資訊；資訊科技。",en:"Common with: collect, provide, look up; information technology."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"某件事、某個人的最新狀況，口語常用。",en:"An update about an event or a person; everyday speech."},{zh:"常搭配：好消息、壞消息、有消息、聽到消息。",en:"Common with: good/bad news, to hear back, to hear word."}],
 exA:[{zh:"做決定之前，先蒐集足夠的資訊。",en:"Gather enough information before you decide."},{zh:"教練會先看客戶填的背景資訊，再準備第一次的對談。",en:"The coach reviews the background information the client filled in before the first session."}],
 exB:[{zh:"好消息：客戶說這次跟主管的對話很成功！",en:"Good news: my client said her conversation with her manager went really well!"},{zh:"上次教練課後，客戶兩個禮拜都沒有消息。",en:"It's been two weeks since our last session and I haven't heard from my client."}],
 contrast:{zh:"課前表單給了我很多資訊，但客戶一見面就先分享了一個好消息。",en:"The intake form gave me a lot of information, but the first thing my client shared in person was good news."},
 swap:[{zh:"我有一個好資訊。",ok:false,en:"Unnatural. Good news is 好消息."},{zh:"資訊科技",ok:true,en:"Fixed term for IT. Never 消息科技."}]},

{a:"清楚",b:"明確",pa:"qīngchu",pb:"míngquè",ga:"clear, easy to understand",gb:"explicit, definite",
 shared:{zh:"都有「不模糊」的意思。",en:"Both mean \"not vague.\" 清楚 is about being easy to see or understand; 明確 is about leaving no room for doubt."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"看得清楚、聽得清楚、說得清楚：容易理解。",en:"Easy to see, hear, or follow."},{zh:"也可以說「我不清楚」＝我不知道。",en:"「我不清楚」 means \"I'm not sure / I don't know.\""}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"目標、方向、立場、界線很確定，沒有模糊空間。",en:"Goals, direction, stance, or boundaries that are firm and specific."},{zh:"比較正式，常用在工作場合。",en:"More formal; common at work."}],
 exA:[{zh:"你說得很清楚，我完全聽懂了。",en:"You explained it clearly; I understood completely."},{zh:"這件事我不太清楚，要問一下主管。",en:"I'm not sure about this; I need to check with my manager."}],
 exB:[{zh:"教練幫她訂出明確的目標：三個月內，每週跟團隊成員做一次一對一。",en:"The coach helped her set a concrete goal: a weekly one-on-one with each team member for three months."},{zh:"她明確地拒絕了加班的要求。",en:"She clearly and firmly declined the overtime request."}],
 contrast:{zh:"他的簡報講得很清楚，但下一步還不夠明確。",en:"His presentation was clear, but the next steps weren't specific enough."},
 swap:[{zh:"這件事我不太明確。",ok:false,en:"Wrong. \"I'm not sure\" is 我不太清楚."},{zh:"主管的指示很清楚／很明確。",ok:true,en:"Both work. 清楚 = easy to follow; 明確 = specific, no ambiguity."}]},

{a:"緊張",b:"焦慮",pa:"jǐnzhāng",pb:"jiāolǜ",ga:"nervous, tense",gb:"anxious, worried",
 shared:{zh:"都是不安的情緒。",en:"Both describe unease. 緊張 is usually tied to a specific moment; 焦慮 is a longer, deeper worry about the future."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"面對某個場合的當下反應，通常短暫。",en:"A reaction to a specific event, usually short-lived."},{zh:"也可以形容情況：時間很緊張、關係很緊張。",en:"Also describes situations: a tight schedule, strained relations."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"對不確定的未來一直擔心，持續比較久。",en:"Ongoing worry about an uncertain future."},{zh:"可以當名詞：職涯焦慮、焦慮感。",en:"Also a noun: career anxiety, a sense of anxiety."}],
 exA:[{zh:"第一次跟副總報告，我緊張得手都在發抖。",en:"Presenting to the VP for the first time, my hands were shaking from nerves."},{zh:"專案時間很緊張，大家都在加班。",en:"The project timeline is tight and everyone is working late."}],
 exB:[{zh:"很多客戶第一次來找教練時，心裡都帶著對未來的焦慮。",en:"Many clients come to their first coaching session carrying anxiety about the future."},{zh:"接下新角色的焦慮很常見，教練會幫你找到可以掌控的部分。",en:"Anxiety about taking on a new role is common; a coach helps you find what you can control."}],
 contrast:{zh:"簡報前緊張很正常，但如果每天都睡不好，那可能是焦慮。",en:"Being nervous before a presentation is normal, but if you can't sleep every night, that may be anxiety."},
 swap:[{zh:"時間很焦慮。",ok:false,en:"Wrong. A tight schedule is 時間很緊張."},{zh:"我對帶新團隊這件事有點緊張／焦慮。",ok:true,en:"Both work. 焦慮 sounds more serious and lasting."}]},

{a:"理解",b:"了解",pa:"lǐjiě",pb:"liǎojiě",ga:"to comprehend; to empathize",gb:"to know about; to find out",
 shared:{zh:"都可以翻成 understand。",en:"Both translate as \"understand.\" 了解 is knowing about something; 理解 is grasping the why, or accepting someone's feelings."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"懂背後的道理、原因、意思，比較深。",en:"Grasping the reasoning or meaning behind something."},{zh:"也有「體諒」的意思：我能理解你的感受。",en:"Also means to empathize: I understand how you feel."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"知道、熟悉某個人、某件事的情況。",en:"To know about or be familiar with a person or situation."},{zh:"也可以當「去弄清楚」：了解一下。",en:"Also \"to find out\": 了解一下 = look into it."}],
 exA:[{zh:"我能理解你為什麼對這次的回饋感到挫折。",en:"I can understand why this feedback felt frustrating to you."},{zh:"這篇文章很難，我讀了三次才理解。",en:"This article is hard; I read it three times before I understood it."}],
 exB:[{zh:"我想先了解一下你目前的工作狀況。",en:"First I'd like to learn about your current work situation."},{zh:"我跟他共事五年，很了解他的做事風格。",en:"I've worked with him for five years; I know his style well."}],
 contrast:{zh:"我了解公司的新規定，但我不理解為什麼要這樣規定。",en:"I know what the new policy is, but I don't understand why it was made."},
 swap:[{zh:"我們先理解一下客戶的需求。",ok:false,en:"Unnatural. \"Let's find out\" is 了解一下."},{zh:"我能理解你的難處。",ok:true,en:"Empathy uses 理解, not 了解."}]},

{a:"結構",b:"架構",pa:"jiégòu",pb:"jiàgòu",ga:"structure, composition",gb:"framework, architecture",
 shared:{zh:"都跟「組成方式」有關。",en:"Both describe how something is organized. 結構 is how the parts fit together; 架構 is the overall frame someone designs."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"內部各部分怎麼組成、比例如何。",en:"How the internal parts are composed or proportioned."},{zh:"常搭配：句子結構、文章結構、人口結構。",en:"Common with: sentence, essay, population structure."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"整體的框架、骨架，常是設計出來的。",en:"The overall skeleton or framework, usually designed."},{zh:"常搭配：系統架構、思考架構、組織架構圖。",en:"Common with: system architecture, thinking framework, org chart."}],
 exA:[{zh:"這篇文章結構很清楚：先講問題，再講方法。",en:"This essay is well structured: problem first, then solution."},{zh:"我們團隊的年齡結構越來越年輕。",en:"Our team's age makeup is getting younger."}],
 exB:[{zh:"教練常用 GROW 架構來引導對話。",en:"Coaches often use the GROW framework to guide a conversation."},{zh:"公司重組後，組織架構圖全部重畫了。",en:"After the reorg, the whole org chart was redrawn."}],
 contrast:{zh:"用一個好的思考架構，你的回答結構自然就會清楚。",en:"With a good thinking framework, your answer's structure will naturally be clear."},
 swap:[{zh:"這個句子的架構不對。",ok:false,en:"Grammar uses 結構: 句子結構."},{zh:"組織結構／組織架構",ok:true,en:"Both used. 架構 feels more like the org chart; 結構 more like the makeup."}]},

{a:"記憶",b:"回憶",pa:"jìyì",pb:"huíyì",ga:"memory (ability or stored content)",gb:"recollection; to recall",
 shared:{zh:"都跟過去記得的事有關。",en:"Both relate to the past. 記憶 is the ability or stored memory; 回憶 is looking back, often with feeling."},
 pa_pts:[{zh:"大腦記住東西的能力，或記住的內容，比較中性。",en:"The ability to remember, or what is stored; neutral."},{zh:"常搭配：記憶力、在我的記憶中。",en:"Common with: memory (ability), in my memory."}],
 pb_pts:[{zh:"主動想起過去的經驗，常帶感情。",en:"Actively thinking back on past experiences, often emotional."},{zh:"也可以當動詞：回憶一下、回憶起。",en:"Also a verb: think back, recall."}],
 exA:[{zh:"我的記憶力越來越差，單字要多複習幾次。",en:"My memory is getting worse; I need to review vocabulary more often."},{zh:"在我的記憶中，那是第一次帶團隊。",en:"As far as I remember, that was the first time I led a team."}],
 exB:[{zh:"第一次帶教練團體課，留下了很多美好的回憶。",en:"Leading my first group coaching program left many good memories."},{zh:"請你回憶一下，上次覺得工作很有成就感是什麼時候？",en:"Think back: when did you last feel real accomplishment at work?"}],
 contrast:{zh:"我的記憶不太好，但那次升遷是我最難忘的回憶。",en:"My memory isn't great, but that promotion is my most unforgettable memory."},
